WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.500
- [Narrator] It's been six
whole years since the finale

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.250
of Breaking Bad aired and we still can't

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.540
stop thinking about it.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.700
It was the obsessive attention to detail

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.130
that catapulted the show
to the history books

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.523
as one of the greatest of all time.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.330
- Say my name.

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:18.010
- [Narrator] Every detail in Breaking Bad

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.810
is intentional but they
can be easy to overlook

00:00:20.810 --> 00:00:23.190
if you've only watched through once.

00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.310
So why don't we take a look
at some of the hidden details

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:27.783
of Breaking Bad that
you might have missed.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.460
In an interview wit GQ,

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.337
show creator, Vince Gilligan, said

00:00:33.337 --> 00:00:35.427
"I obsess a great deal more than I should

00:00:35.427 --> 00:00:38.850
"over those details, I
sweat the small stuff."

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:42.000
It's clear that Vince and team
always had a complete vision

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.580
of the shows story from start to finish

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.310
and that is particularly evident

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.193
in the use of foreshadowing.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.950
Breaking Bad is stuffed full
of clues that give hints

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:53.230
for what's to come.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:55.580
For example, remember these intro teasers

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.880
scattered throughout season two?

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:01.530
We now know that it was the
debris from the Wayfarer 515

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.580
crash in the season finale,

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.500
even if at the time we had no idea

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.470
what this pink teddy bear was

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:10.680
but the clues were always there.

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:15.245
The teasers kick off episodes
one, four, 10 and 13,

00:01:15.245 --> 00:01:20.245
titled Seven Thirty Seven,
Down, Over and ABQ respectively,

00:01:20.910 --> 00:01:24.716
combine them and we'd know
exactly what was going to happen.

00:01:24.716 --> 00:01:27.799
(explosion overhead)

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:36.550
Not all of the foreshadowing
was quite as cryptic though,

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:38.240
the shows cinematography prepares us

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.150
for eventually character
and plots developments.

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:43.350
These include hinting at Walt's future

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.570
with Tuco's perfectly fitting grill,

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:48.880
and with a carefully place
bullet hole in Walt's reflection,

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:50.620
as well as the white
king on the chessboard

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:53.790
in Ozymandias being
dangerously close to checkmate.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:55.920
Here's a dark example for you,

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.490
in the season two episode titled Phoenix,

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:00.660
Walt turns over his
newborn daughter, Holly,

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.203
just in case she spits up.

00:02:03.068 --> 00:02:06.155
- Just in case she decides
to do a little spit up,

00:02:06.155 --> 00:02:08.860
we'll roll up and nice,
clean towel like this

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:09.710
and put it under.

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:13.170
- [Narrator] Well, later
in the same episode,

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:15.840
when faced with a similar
situation with Jane,

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.712
he makes a very different choice.

00:02:18.712 --> 00:02:21.295
(Jane choking)

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:35.150
Much of the foreshadowing
has been confirmed

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:37.810
by Vince Gilligan but eagle eyed fans

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.690
think they've spotted more.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:42.630
Take this shot, Saul
Goodman's license plate

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.910
which usually reads as lawyer up,

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:47.810
is partially obscured by Walt and Jesse,

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.340
now it reads wire up.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.830
Can you guess what happened next?

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:53.390
- But you're here for answers, okay?

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:56.320
But don't push the questions,

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.230
okay, let's not get him
suspicious, all right?

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:00.840
- [Narrator] This scene from season two,

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.370
where Walt and Jesse are
stranded out in the desert

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:06.780
has also sparked speculation from fans.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:07.930
- What are we building?

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.755
- You said it yourself.

00:03:10.755 --> 00:03:11.588
- A robot?

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:13.840
- A battery.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.540
- [Narrator] Well, it turns
out in the series finale,

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:19.080
Walt kind of does build
a robot to get themselves

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:21.401
out of another sticky situation.

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:23.395
(car alarm beeps)

00:03:23.395 --> 00:03:26.395
(machine gun fires)

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.390
It's just just foreshadowing
that shows us how intentional

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:36.510
Breaking Bad is with details though,

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.928
the shows use of symmetry
demonstrates the progression

00:03:38.928 --> 00:03:40.873
of plot and character.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.500
Let's start at the beginning

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:45.900
with Walt and Jesse's
first meeting in the show.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:53.220
- [Walt] Hey, it's me, I'm alone.

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:54.120
- [Narrator] And now,

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.070
the last time they ever see each other.

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:06.320
The parallels are clear between the shots

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:08.380
and allow us to reminisce about how far

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.050
these characters have come.

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.980
This is particularly evident with Jesse,

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:16.070
throughout the show, he's
always the passenger,

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:18.270
that is, until the series finale,

00:04:18.270 --> 00:04:20.940
when he finally breaks
free and becomes the driver

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:22.835
of his own destiny.

00:04:22.835 --> 00:04:25.585
(Jesse laughing)

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.150
That's not the only reflective
shot in the finale though,

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:31.650
the final shot of Breaking Bad

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:34.240
shows us the death of
Heisenberg the drug lord

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.650
and echos a shot in season four

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:40.013
where the Walter White we knew
is consumed by Heisenberg.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:44.450
We also get a call back
to the very first shot

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.710
later in the series.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:47.300
Walt's trousers flying through the air

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.310
is now an iconic image, where did they go?

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:52.253
Well, look closely.

00:04:52.253 --> 00:04:54.526
♪ Take my true love by her hand ♪

00:04:54.526 --> 00:04:58.256
♪ Lead her through the town ♪

00:04:58.256 --> 00:04:59.145
(track rewinds)

00:04:59.145 --> 00:05:01.358
♪ Love by her hand ♪

00:05:01.358 --> 00:05:03.650
♪ Lead her through the town ♪

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.100
This one is really great,

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:07.060
if Skyler's reaction to her legal trouble

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:10.123
seems familiar to you,
that's because it is.

00:05:11.314 --> 00:05:14.231
(muffled speaking)

00:05:17.473 --> 00:05:18.306
- Is she even listening?

00:05:18.306 --> 00:05:19.990
- [Narrator] It's almost an exact replica

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:23.753
of Walt receiving his cancer
diagnosis in the pilot.

00:05:23.753 --> 00:05:26.730
(muffled speaking)

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:27.780
- [Doctor] Mr. White?

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:30.463
- Yes.

00:05:30.463 --> 00:05:32.020
- [Narrator] What about this shot of Walt

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:34.160
sitting by the pool with his son.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.670
- [Walt] Should of brought our suits, huh?

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:37.893
- [Narrator] It feels like
we might have seen it before.

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:42.320
Breaking Bad is a visually orientated show

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.770
and many of the hidden details

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:46.513
are a result of carefully
planned production design.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.680
Clothing, in particular, gives us insight

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.150
in to character progression.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:53.730
In the first couple of seasons,

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:56.550
Walt goes from wearing
brighter colors such a beige

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:59.400
and green to dark browns and black,

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:03.330
reflecting his increasingly
dark actions and state of mind.

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:06.370
This is also the same
with Skyler and Hank,

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:07.600
who moved to darker colors

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:10.160
from blue and orange respectively.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.450
Not Marie though, she
just really loves purple.

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:16.390
Details are also hidden in various props.

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:17.300
In the final episode,

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.900
the camera lingers on this
New Hampshire license plate

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:23.020
and it's state motto, live free or die.

00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:25.370
This tells us the outcome
of the two main characters

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:27.180
at the end of episode,

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:30.780
one lives free, while the
other, well, you know the rest.

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.120
This one is extremely meta,

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:35.110
notice anything about this shot?

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:38.010
Yep, that's right, it's the shows logo

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:40.190
based on the elements
in the periodic table

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:41.940
hiding in plain sight.

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:43.053
And here it is again.

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:46.970
The shows final episode has been subject

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:49.590
to much of the search for hidden details.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.000
It's called Felina,

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.730
which besides being an anagram for finale,

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:57.620
is also the subject for a song
at the start of the episode.

00:06:57.620 --> 00:06:59.800
As Walt drives back to New Mexico,

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:03.193
he listens to a song called
"El Paso" by Marty Robbins.

00:07:04.406 --> 00:07:07.460
♪ And at last here I am on the hill ♪

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:09.670
It tells of a man who returns to the town

00:07:09.670 --> 00:07:11.520
where he is a wanted man to find

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:14.240
the woman he loves called Felina.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:15.920
If that wasn't obscure enough for you,

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:18.200
the coordinates of the spot
that Walt buries the money

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.890
are actually those of Q Studios
in Albuquerque, New Mexico,

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:23.660
where the show was filmed.

00:07:23.660 --> 00:07:28.660
- 34, 59, 20, 106, 36, 52,
34, 59, 20, 106, 36, 52.

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.320
- [Narrator] I think we
have time for one more.

00:07:32.320 --> 00:07:34.230
There's a theory that
Walt picks up the traits

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:36.620
of every person in the
series that he kills

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:39.130
and this is certainly
backed up in the details.

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:41.595
There's the crustless
sandwiches from Krazy-8,

00:07:41.595 --> 00:07:42.700
- [Woman] We're going
to take a little time

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:45.390
out of our schedule to gather in the gym.

00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:47.490
- [Narrator] The vomiting ritual from Gus,

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:11.277
and his changed taste in drinks from Mike.

00:08:11.277 --> 00:08:16.070
- Uh, another round for him
and I'll have the same, no ice.

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:16.903
- Rocks, right?

00:08:16.903 --> 00:08:17.736
- Rocks, yes.

00:08:17.736 --> 00:08:20.570
- [Narrator] He even straight
up takes some lines from Mike.

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:23.580
- Do yourself a favor and learn
to take yes for an answer.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:25.190
- Trust me, if you do this--

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:28.120
- Lydia, learn to take yes for an answer.

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:29.850
- [Narrator] Well, that's a lot to process

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:32.940
and we haven't even scratched the surface.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.370
There's a reason we're all
so obsessed with Breaking Bad

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:38.940
to this day, these hidden
details are truly the gift

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:40.620
that keeps on giving.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.023
Vince and team, we salute you.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:45.503
- You're goddamn right!

00:08:46.564 --> 00:08:49.731
(gentle upbeat music)

